    "body": "claimed: austin62jake (Claude Code session) · 2026-11-08T10:52:21Z · branch issue/228-seam-columns (fork austin62jake/Camcraft) · fix up as draft PR #284 (I should have posted this claim before starting - sorry). Cause: not a 1e-9 tolerance alone - the axis fit leaned the two-ring bar by rounding. Every side facet of a two-ring bar anchors its normal line at the bar's mid-station, so the refinement's tilt rows see nothing; the eigen axis was exactly Z (residual 7.4e-14) and the refinement returned a 2.6e-5 rad tilt (n 16) that the fit kept on a residual lower by noise. The fix skips refining an already-concurrent eigen line, groups seam columns at the weld grain (1e-6 rad), and makes the refusal name a mixed column count as well as a feature. Pinned in `motion/tests/rotary_dflat.rs` (three tests that fail on main); batch gate 2400 tests pass, only the three Windows pixel snapshots fail, as on main.",
